      },
      "schema:alternateName": [
        "カンナビゲロール酸 (CBGA)",
        "CBGA",
        "CBGa"
      ],
      "schema:description": "`CBGa` is the owner's term for **cannabigerolic acid** (standard spelling CBGA), confirmed by the owner on 2026-11-11. Identity and identifiers were verified against ChEBI 67081 (cannabigerolic acid), Wikidata Q27135612 (en label 'cannabigerolic acid', CAS 25555-57-1, PubChem CID 6449999, ChEBI 67081, formula C22H32O4), the FDA GSRS record for UNII 80I4ZM847Y (substanceClass chemical, definitionLevel COMPLETE; names CANNABIGEROLIC ACID / CBGA; CAS 25555-57-1, PubChem CID 6449999, formula C22H32O4) and PubChem CID 6449999 ('Cannabigerolic Acid', C22H32O4). The owner's spelling `CBGa` (lowercase 'a') is preserved exactly in the labels and in the registered query strings; it names the same substance as CBGA, is not a second substance, and no case normalization is applied to raw or query records. CBGA is an acidic phytocannabinoid and the biosynthetic precursor from which other cannabinoid acids are formed (ChEBI: 'a biosynthetic precursor to delta-9-tetrahydrocannabinol'; PMID 31686510 describes the phytocannabinoid acids, including CBGA, as the dominant forms in the plant; PMID 35887277). CBG is the decarboxylated neutral product of CBGA, not a synonym: heating converts CBGA to CBG (PMID 35887277; PMID 36397993), so the two are recorded as distinct concepts. Placement in compound-minor records only 'a phytocannabinoid other than the major pair'; no chemical-class link is asserted and no regulatory status is claimed. **No skos:related link to compound_cbg is asserted:** the precursor/product relation is recorded in this note only, and the compound_cbg external-identifier mapping is unresolved (separate follow-up). **Query limitation:** Google Trends and YouTube series for `CBGa` measure occurrences of that literal string, not verified cannabigerolic acid content; the two Google Trends attempts returned no series (NO_DATA), and the existing samples are string-match observations. Basis and source record: docs/provenance/compound-taxonomy.md (ISS-20261111-TAX-040 addendum).",
      "schema:termCode": "compound_cbga"
    },
